ess\"","Plan intentionally replaces empty stdout with a confirmation line but does not classify this as a breaking change to the silent-output contract nor discuss back-out"],"finding":"The plan changes the stdout contract of currently-silent verbs (they now emit a confirmation line), which can break scripts/consumers that rely on empty stdout as a success signal (e.g. `test -z \"$(rebar link ...)\"` or piping stdout). The plan offers `--quiet` as an escape hatch but never acknowledges this as a behavior change to an existing (silent) output contract, nor states a rollback/back-out consideration.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5a764e829c57b25e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Why / Step 1 / Scope IN","norm_id":"n0c9fb69d4d1660c6","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A wrapper script asserting empty stdout on `rebar tag` now sees a confirmation line and reports spurious failure"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a short compat note to Scope: 'This is an intentional, additive-but-observable change to the silent-verb stdout contract; scripts depending on empty stdout use --quiet. No data/schema change — fully reversible by reverting the commit.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_ra